From: Mansur Aliyu <mansurmasama@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 12:26:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Disable the generic inactivity stop while the transaction
 window is active

Prepared with Claude (Anthropic's AI assistant) and tested on Lan's pilot rows.

With the transaction window, warm-up and the measurement blocks after the
window contain only block events. The generic inactivity stop (no event for
BCI + 30 min) then fires on ordinary gaps between blocks: at BCI = 1200 s a gap
above 3000 s has probability ~8% per block, so long warm-ups almost always
stopped. Before the window, continuous transaction events hid this.

With the window enabled, stalls are now detected only by the canonical-progress
guard (-Dthreesim.canonicalProgressStallMs) and the workload guards. Without
the window the behaviour is unchanged.

verify_pilot_results.py additionally flags INACTIVITY stops under the window
and realizations where the attackers hold the majority of hashing power.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VW4BVs5G9Z88DX5W1xG1Ma
---
 .../threesim/monitoring/ThreesimSimulationMonitor.kt   | 10 +++++++++-
 .../pilot_tools/verify_pilot_results.py                |  5 +++++
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/3sim/org.palladiosimulator.blockchainsystems.threesim/src/main/kotlin/org/palladiosimulator/blockchainsystems/threesim/monitoring/ThreesimSimulationMonitor.kt b/3sim/org.palladiosimulator.blockchainsystems.threesim/src/main/kotlin/org/palladiosimulator/blockchainsystems/threesim/monitoring/ThreesimSimulationMonitor.kt
index d7bd1242..3bf0dba6 100644
--- a/3sim/org.palladiosimulator.blockchainsystems.threesim/src/main/kotlin/org/palladiosimulator/blockchainsystems/threesim/monitoring/ThreesimSimulationMonitor.kt
+++ b/3sim/org.palladiosimulator.blockchainsystems.threesim/src/main/kotlin/org/palladiosimulator/blockchainsystems/threesim/monitoring/ThreesimSimulationMonitor.kt
@@ -1156,7 +1156,15 @@ class ThreesimSimulationMonitor(
       }
     }
 
-    if (inactivityThresholdCondition.hasProlongedInactivityExceeded()) {
+    // With the transaction window, warm-up and the part of measurement after the
+    // window contain only block events. The generic inactivity limit (BCI + 30 min
+    // without any event) is then routinely exceeded by ordinary gaps between
+    // blocks: at BCI = 1200 s, a gap longer than 3000 s occurs with probability
+    // e^-2.5 ~ 8% per block, so long warm-ups almost always stopped. Before the
+    // window, continuous transaction events masked this. A stalled run is instead
+    // detected by the canonical-progress guard (-Dthreesim.canonicalProgressStallMs)
+    // and the workload guards. Without the window the old behaviour is unchanged.
+    if (!transactionWindowEnabled && inactivityThresholdCondition.hasProlongedInactivityExceeded()) {
       return markTermination("INACTIVITY", false)
     }
     return false
diff --git a/trilemma/org.palladiosimulator.blockchainsystems.trilemma/pilot_tools/verify_pilot_results.py b/trilemma/org.palladiosimulator.blockchainsystems.trilemma/pilot_tools/verify_pilot_results.py
index 73c0930f..cf1ee360 100644
--- a/trilemma/org.palladiosimulator.blockchainsystems.trilemma/pilot_tools/verify_pilot_results.py
+++ b/trilemma/org.palladiosimulator.blockchainsystems.trilemma/pilot_tools/verify_pilot_results.py
@@ -71,6 +71,11 @@ def main():
                 print(f'[WARN] {p.name}: kappa_tx_warm = {audit.get("transactionWarmupBlocks")} (manuscript: 30)')
             if complete and int(audit.get('transactionWindowEndTimeMs',0) or 0) <= 0:
                 print(f'[FAIL] {p.name}: run complete but transaction window end not recorded'); good=False
+        q_a=creation.get('realizedAdversarialHashingPowerShare')
+        if q_a is not None and float(q_a) >= 0.5:
+            print(f'[WARN] {p.name}: attackers hold {float(q_a):.2f} of hashing power (majority); selfish mining becomes a majority takeover')
+        if audit.get('terminationReason') == 'INACTIVITY' and audit.get('transactionWindowEnabled'):
+            print(f'[FAIL] {p.name}: INACTIVITY stop with the transaction window (jar predates the inactivity fix)'); good=False
         if audit.get('terminationReason','').startswith('WORKLOAD_LIMIT'):
             print(f'[WARN] {p.name}: stopped by execution guard {audit["terminationReason"]} in phase {audit.get("executionPhaseAtTermination")}')
         rid=inp.get('network_realization_id')
